From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Mon, 09 Nov 2026 16:18:17 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: skip unconnected stations after a channel
 switch

mac80211 iterates every uploaded station after a channel switch, also
a station that is authenticated and not yet associated. The driver
sends the first station record at association, so the firmware has no
entry for such a station. The beamforming and rate control records
then name a WLAN index that the firmware does not hold.

Skip a station link that is not connected, as the rate control work
does.

Fixes: 3b11a2351769 ("wifi: mt76: mt7996: set specific BSSINFO and STAREC commands after channel switch")
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7996/mcu.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
@@ -3382,7 +3382,7 @@ void mt7996_mcu_update_sta_rec_bw(void *
 		return;
 
 	msta_link = mt7996_sta_link_protected(dev, msta, link_id);
-	if (!msta_link)
+	if (!msta_link || !msta_link->connected)
 		return;
 
 	vif = container_of((void *)msta->vif, struct ieee80211_vif, drv_priv);
